or env vars documented as booleans/numbers, to find readers that don't handle the documented `false`/`0`.\n\n`import.meta.env` result: **zero occurrences anywhere in the repo.** All env access is `process.env`.\n\n---\n\n## Root cause that colors everything\n\n`/Users/mayansharma/Documents/1mg/catalyst-core/packages/catalyst-core/src/scripts/loadEnvironmentVariables.js:26`\n\n```js\nprocess.env = newConfig\n```\n\n`loadEnvironmentVariables()` builds `newConfig` from `config/config.json` (line 16-19) and **replaces the entire `process.env` object** with a plain JS object. Only `typeof === \"object\"` values get `JSON.stringify`'d (line 18) — primitives keep their native JS type. So after this runs, `process.env.NODE_SERVER_PORT` is the **number** `3005` and `process.env.ANALYZE_BUNDLE` is the **boolean** `false`, not strings.\n\nThis is why the known-broken `OTEL_ENABLE === true` sites don't crash — they're reading from a fake env object where booleans survive. It also means:\n- Any real shell env var not listed in `filterKeys` is **wiped** (PATH, HOME, secrets, orchestrator-injected vars).\n- Readers are written against two mutually incompatible type contracts depending on whether they run before or after `preServerInit.js:12`.\n\nEvery finding below is a consequence of, or interacts with, this.\n\n---\n\n## Findings (packages/, src/, scripts/)\n\n### 1. `IS_DEV_COMMAND` written as a JS boolean into a real `spawn` env — silently becomes `\"false\"`\n\n**File:line:** `/Users/mayansharma/Documents/1mg/catalyst-core/packages/catalyst-core/src/scripts/start.js:32`\n**Expression:** `IS_DEV_COMMAND: false,` (inside `spawnSync(..., { env: { ... } })`)\n**Env var:** `IS_DEV_COMMAND`\n\n**Also:** `/Users/mayansharma/Documents/1mg/catalyst-core/packages/catalyst-core/src/scripts/serve.js:38` — identical expression.\n\n**Why it's wrong:** Node's `child_process` coerces every `env` value to a string before `execve`. The boolean `false` written here arrives in the child as the *