          "input": {
            "content": "# API freeze: status, decisions and branch context\n\nCompanion to `api-freeze-implementation.md` (the task breakdown) and `api-freeze-discussion.md` (discussion #402). This file tracks what has actually been decided and built.\n\nLast updated: 2026-08-19.\n\n## Branch strategy\n\nStacked branches. Each phase branch is cut from the previous one, PRs target the parent, and the integration branch merges to main once at the end.\n\n```\nmain\n└─ feat/api-freeze                       integration branch, merges to main last\n   └─ feat/api-freeze-p1-bugfixes       tasks 1, 3, 2 (done, in working tree)\n      └─ feat/api-freeze-p2-public-api  tasks 4, 5, 8 (next)\n         └─ feat/api-freeze-p3-hooks    tasks 6, 7 (blocked on #402 decision)\n            └─ feat/api-freeze-p4-typescript  task 9\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- Dashes, not nested slashes: git cannot have `feat/api-freeze` and `feat/api-freeze/p1` at the same time.\n- A fix for an earlier phase lands on that phase's branch; run `git rebase --update-refs` from the stack tip to ripple it through descendants.\n- If main moves, rebase only `feat/api-freeze`, then ripple the same way.\n- Merge order: p1 into `feat/api-freeze`, rebase and merge each later phase in sequence, then `feat/api-freeze` into main as the single freeze payload.\n- Phase 1 commits are task-scoped: one each for tasks 1, 3, 2, plus one for docs and `.gitignore`.\n\n## Decisions made\n\n- Module aliases: the app's alias wins over Catalyst's at all three merge sites, with no collision warning. One shared function (`src/vite/moduleAliases.js`) owns reading and merging; path resolution stays at call sites.\n- SSR stubs for native hooks return the full key set of the real hook. Function keys are silent no-ops (no dev warnings). This is the standing pattern for task 6 across all 15 hooks.\n- In SSR stubs, `isNative` is `false` and `isWeb` is `true`. `isWeb` means \"not native\" in this codebase (`useBaseHook.js`), and the server pre-renders for web clients, so `true` avoids hydration mismatches on the dominant path. `undefined` was rejected: it is falsy (same as the old bug) and would create a three-state contract. If apps need to detect the server, that is a separate `isSSR` flag to consider in task 6.\n- State keys in stubs mirror the base hook's initial values exactly (`progress` is the full idle object, not null).\n- OTEL_ENABLE fix was reverted. It works in production because `loadEnvironmentVariables()` replaces `process.env` with `config.json` values and JSON types survive, so `=== true` passes for boolean config values. Instead of changing code, this became documented behavior (see below).\n- The `process.env` replacement is now the documented contract: `config.json` types survive into `process.env`, and shell variables are not carried into the server process. Documented in `docs/content/02-Guides and Tutorials/01-First Catalyst App/05-Environment-Variables.md`.\n- No unit tests for phase 1 work (team decision; tests written during implementation were removed).\n- `examples/useai` migration is out of scope for phase 1.\n- `src/scripts/validator.js` deleted wholesale. Its unenforced \"no catalyst keyword in aliases\" rule dies with it; task 7 can resurrect it deliberately.\n- Release versioning and PR mechanics are deferred until the work is done.\n\n## Phase 1: implemented\n\nAll changes are in the working tree, reviewer-approved, not yet committed.\n\nTask 1, crashes and environment bugs:\n\n- `useNotification.js`: all hooks (useState and the large useEffect) hoisted above the SSR return and WebBridge throw. SSR stub expanded from 15 to 23 keys, matching the real return key for key.\n- `useVideoStream.js`: all four return branches (SSR, disabled, web fallback, native) return the identical 15-key set. SSR branch uses `base.webFallbackActive` rather than a hardcoded false.\n- `terminalProgress.js` renamed to `TerminalProgress.js`, matching the class name and all four importers. The first attempt left both casings in the git index (a latent Linux checkout bug); fixed with `git rm --cached`, one entry remains.\n- The OTEL_ENABLE item was implemented, then reverted as unnecessary (see decisions).\n\nTask 3, dead code:\n\n- Deleted `src/native/bridge/standardizedHooks.js` (669 lines), `src/router.js`, `src/scripts/validator.js` (149 lines). Zero importers verified independently twice, including exports map and npm pack surface.\n- Removed the dead commented import in `loadEnvironmentVariables.js` and the dangling `.gitignore` negation for the deleted `router.js`.\n- `src/server/utils/validator.js` is a different, live file and was not touched.\n\nTask 2, module alias resolution:\n\n- Before: `vite.config.js` let Catalyst's aliases win while the SSR runtime loader and the cache-key plugin let the app's win. The cache-key plugin could compute keys against a different file than the bundler resolved within the same build.\n- Now: new `src/vite/moduleAliases.js` exports `getModuleAliases(appRoot)`, merged app-last, used at all three sites. About 60 net lines of duplicated package.json reading removed.\n\nCorrections that came out of review rounds, for the record: the ponytail critique caught the incomplete hook hoist and stub type mismatches; the external reviewer caught the broken rename index state, `isWeb: false` being wrong, and the `progress` shape. The `isWeb === !isNative` invariant from `useBaseHook.js` is the reasoning anchor for stub values.\n\n## Known follow-ups (not blockers)\n\n- Changelog note for whoever cuts the release: apps relying on Catalyst's alias winning in `vite.config.js` for a redefined `@catalyst/template` see the app's file win now.\n- `render.js:18` does `JSON.parse(IS_DEV_COMMAND)` unguarded; throws per request on undefined or non-JSON values. The documented producers (`devBuild`/`devServe`) no longer exist.\n- `src/logger.js`: documented `ENABLE_DEBUG_LOGS`/`ENABLE_CONSOLE_LOGGING` have no readers; debug logging is effectively always on in production, contradicting docs.\n- `ANALYZE_BUNDLE` is required by the startup validator and documented, but nothing reads it. Webpack-era leftover.\n- `start.js`/`serve.js` pass `IS_DEV_COMMAND: false` (a boolean) into a spawn env, which stringifies to a truthy `\"false\"`.\n- `render.js:16` interpolates two asset env vars with no fallback; unset values produce `undefinedundefined/...` asset URLs in SSR HTML.\n- The env vars table in the docs lists three variables no code reads.\n- `mcp_v2/knowledge-base.json` still references deleted files; needs a sync pass.\n- Task 6's blocking decision (what `execute` means for the four multi-action hooks) is still open on discussion #402.\n",
